<Layout title="About Quiet Tools — An Independent App Studio" description="Meet Quiet Tools, the independent studio behind practical apps for hobbies, home maintenance, meal costs, road trips, and homestead planning.">
<section class="page-hero"><p class="section-eyebrow">About Quiet Tools</p><h1>Small software.<br />Everyday purpose.</h1><p>Quiet Tools is an independent app studio making practical software for the details of everyday life.</p></section>
<div class="article-body"><h2>Start with something useful.</h2><p>A repair you want to remember. A hobby you made time for. The cost of a meal, or a game that makes the drive more fun. Our apps begin with things people already do and give those details a place to belong.</p><h2>One app, a clear purpose.</h2><p>Each app focuses on its own job. You can choose a personal hobby journal, household records, equipment maintenance, food budgeting, shared road-trip games, or homestead planning.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/apps/">Explore the Quiet Tools apps ↗</a></p><h2>Understand what you are using.</h2><p>Product pages explain features and availability. Each app has its own support and privacy information, so you can check the details that matter before you start.</p><p><a href="/privacy/">Read our privacy overview</a> or <a href="/support/">find support for your app</a>.</p><h2>Get in touch.</h2><p>Questions and thoughtful feedback are welcome at <a href="mailto:support@quiettoolsapps.com">support@quiettoolsapps.com</a>.</p></div>
</Layout>
